<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies 12 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies 12 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 12 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--San Francisco Airports, Calif., $275 million revenue bonds.  </p>
<p>Includes $110 million non-AMT and $165 million AMT bonds.</p>
<p>--North Brandford, Conn., $9.6 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Hancock County, Miss., $3.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Madison, Miss., $1 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hoke County, N.C., $4.38 million refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Onslow County, N.C., $1.2 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Onslow County, N.C., $20 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Riverside-Beaver School District, Pa., $20 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Springfield School District, Pa., $9.995 million bonds.</p>
<p>--Grapevine, Texas, $2.92 million water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Grapevine, Texas, $9.785 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
